# UX workflow: shared Macro context selector and focalized editors.
# Purpose: proves the same held-NAV grammar as Sequencer: preview while held,
# apply on release, short NAV opens the focused object, LEFT_TOP returns.

0 scenario macro-automation-clean
80 capture screen macro_page_hot_surface

# Page -> Macro: the temporary overlay is visible only while NAV is held.
180 button NAV down
260 encoder NAV 1
340 capture screen macro_context_preview
420 button NAV up
560 capture screen macro_context_applied

# A short NAV opens the focused physical Macro; Back returns to performance.
660 tap NAV 60
900 capture screen macro_editor_open
1000 tap LEFT_TOP 60
1240 capture screen macro_back_to_surface

# Macro -> Page -> Track with the same gesture; Track tap opens Track Editor.
1340 button NAV down
1420 encoder NAV -1
1500 encoder NAV -1
1580 capture screen track_context_preview
1660 button NAV up
1800 tap NAV 60
2040 capture screen track_editor_open
2140 tap LEFT_TOP 60
2380 capture screen track_back_to_macro

# A hold without rotation is inspection-only and never opens legacy Structure.
2480 button NAV down
3560 tick
3640 capture screen held_context_inspection
3720 button NAV up
3960 capture screen held_context_released
